# Search a 2D Matrix

Approach

Step 1

Use Binary Search on the first element of every row to determine the row in which the target can exist.

Step 2

If the target is smaller than the first element of the first row, return false.

Step 3

After the first binary search ends, return left - 1 because left points to the first row whose first element is greater than the target. Therefore, the required row is the previous row.

Step 4

Perform another Binary Search on the identified row.

Step 5

If the target is found, return true. Otherwise, return false.

Note

First Binary Search:
- Search on the first element of every row.
- After the loop ends, left points to the first row whose first element is greater than the target.
- Hence, the correct row is left - 1.

Second Binary Search:
- Perform a normal Binary Search on that row.

Time Complexity

O(log m + log n)

Space Complexity

O(1)